{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmY2keFuWiZFQKenhR7u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved four of the seven rows and returned three, so the batch outcome is `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=7`. The verdict is committed as `ba98b20c` with the `WI: WI-835` trailer, in `docs/reviews/wi-835-coordinator-retained-adjudication/004-ADJUDICATE-6ca0b05.md`.\n\n**Approved (SR-227's chain):**\n- **LLR-305:** the earlier problems are fixed. The entry-point section moved out, the duplicate exit codes and the `session_summary` sentence are gone, and what's left is the shared request and the sign-in probe, both of which SR-227 asks for. LLR-270 owns where the sign-in check is called, and the code matches it.\n- **TC-322:** now checks that a brief class with no template adds nothing, and its Expected covers everything its Method asserts.\n- **TC-323:** unchanged and sound. Its parent is now approved.\n- **TC-324:** now checks that a family with no dedicated home passes without a probe. The lane-only assertions moved out, so Expected and Method agree.\n\n**Returned (SR-231's chain):**\n- **SR-231:** its acceptance asks for creating missing parent directories and for a refusal to release its empty reservation. Its Requirement asks for neither. That's the same problem I returned SR-227 for earlier.\n- **LLR-306:** it carries part of SR-227's work: the coordinator route building the shared request, planning the retention, launching and recording the call, plus the sign-in reading command. But it traces only to SR-231, so no design row that traces to SR-227 covers the coordinator side of SR-227.\n- **TC-321:** it asserts SR-227 behaviour (the coordinator route's recorded retained call, exit 7 on a sign-in refusal) but lists only SR-231 as what it verifies. The split also left two tests cited by no TC: `test_a_second_coordinator_adjudication_resumes_the_first` and `test_a_session_at_the_dial_drains_and_retires_at_the_next_clear_point`. WI-835's Done-when names both.\n\n**What I committed:**\n- **The follow-up:** one draft in a new `## Dispositions` section of the WI-835 spec, committed with the verdict. It parses cleanly and intake will mint it when WI-835 merges.\n- **The approval act** (`ef6de70f`): only those four rows changed from Drafted to Approved, and nothing else in the registries changed. The snapshot copied the LLR and TC registries only, recorded as act 39. I left out the system-requirements token because SR-231, its only row in this batch, was returned.\n\nLLR-306, TC-321 and SR-231 are still Drafted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":995,"cache_read_input_tokens":158026,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":995},"output_tokens":755,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce1fccc0-8fec-4295-889e-541a0dc6f24a","uuid":"64819c12-6d01-4a69-8165-cb0e53202665","timestamp":"2026-10-06T19:28:38.482Z","request_id":"req_011CfmY2kMPfWHBPkgE2Xked"}
